# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_conflict_marker_adversarial.py" "CONFLICT-MARKER ADVERSARIAL GATE: PASS" "conflict-marker detector + Unknown verdict reasoning - adversarial / boundary cases (malformed inputs designed to break invariants)" "conflict-marker detector adversarial boundary gate: pins behavior on malformed / edge / 'looks-like-a-marker-but-isnt' inputs. (A1) marker shape INSIDE a string literal (mid-line, not column 0) - must NOT fire because the line-start gate holds even when a fixture stores the marker shape inside a Python string. (A1b) marker shape preceded by indentation - must NOT fire (gits real markers always sit at column 0; indented marker text is content). (A2) TRUNCATED diff - the head <<<<<<< landed in the patch but the tail >>>>>>> was cut off (GitHubs Files API caps patch payloads); the pair gate must NOT fire on a half-shape. (A2c) sanity that the pair-gate DOES fire when both halves are present (confirms the negatives arent spuriously suppressing real input). (A3) marker shape inside a markdown fenced code block at column 0 IS detected - documents the honest boundary that the detector is LOCAL (sees only diff syntax, not file language); the render escalation uses the honest-softened 'likely git conflict' wording (PO 2026-06-25 #457) so the docs-example FP never becomes a confident overclaim. (B) Unknown-verdict reasoning split: same verdict, distinct reason copy. (B1) new-file Unknown uses 'NEW in this PR' / 'computable after merge' / 'expected, not a warning' framing (no extractor-gap wording). (B2) extractor-gap Unknown uses 'extractor gap' / 'un-indexed' / 'Treat as unknown, not clear' framing (no new-in-PR wording). (B3) the two render-bodies DIFFER (the split is preserved - same verdict, distinguishable reason). (B4) both-causes Unknown renders both paragraphs in semantic order (expected case first, warranted-attention case second). (B5) lumped fallback (added_paths=None) preserves the honesty note for older call sites. PURE + offline (synthetic patches, no DB, no network)" "conflict-marker adversarial gate: marker shape inside a string literal (mid-line) does NOT fire (line-start gate), indented marker text does NOT fire (gits markers are column 0), truncated diff (half a marker shape) does NOT fire (pair gate holds), pair-complete patch DOES fire (sanity), markdown fenced block at column 0 IS detected (documents the honest local boundary) with render copy softened to 'likely git conflict' (no overclaim), Unknown new-file vs extractor-gap render distinct reason strings (B1 / B2 / B3), both-causes Unknown preserves the new-first / gap-second semantic order (B4), lumped fallback when added_paths=None preserves honesty (B5)" 32
